# Goal 7: Fix logb subnormal exponent calculation

## Function
logb (double)

## Source Files
- C: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/logbd.c
- Rust: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/mathd.rs (fn logbd, line ~3103)

## What's Wrong
Output mismatch:
- `logb(0x0.0000000000001p-1022)`: C returns `-0x1.0c8p+10` (-1074.0), Rust returns `-0x1.0ccp+10` (-1075.0)

The subnormal exponent is off by one — same root cause as the ilogb subnormal issue.

## What Needs to Change
Fix the subnormal normalization in logbd. The bit-counting loop or the initial exponent bias produces an exponent that is one too low. Compare with the C logbd.c implementation.

## Success Criteria
- `logb(0x0.0000000000001p-1022)` returns -1074.0 (as `-0x1.0c8p+10`)
- All other logb test cases continue to pass
